## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW & EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

The objective of this engagement is to engineer and deploy a specialized on-demand home healthcare and medical practitioner dispatch platform.

In urban centers across Nigeria, traditional hospital outpatient consultations are hampered by severe traffic gridlock, long hospital waiting times, and overcrowded clinical waiting rooms. For working professionals, elderly parents, chronic illness patients, and mothers with young children, visiting a hospital for routine checkups, nursing care, lab sample collection, or physiotherapy is exhausting and stressful.

This platform bridges that gap by enabling patients and families to easily browse, book, schedule, and pay for accredited medical personnel (general practitioners, registered nurses, certified physiotherapists, and phlebotomists / lab technicians) to deliver healthcare directly in their homes.

The ecosystem provides an intuitive, friction-free booking flow for patients while offering medical professionals clear visit itineraries, automated fee collection, and giving the business owner comprehensive clinical oversight and commission tracking.

